een akame and ez death be  anything but a death match for 23  episodes we've seen what the two  fighters are capable of and it's finally  time for the inevitable collision  emotions are running high following  tatsumi's death and both agame and  ezdeth  open right up with their iconic  techniques it seems that the tides have  turned in favour of esdeath who was on  the defensive the majority of the fight  only for her to get struck by a decisive  blow  accepting defeat she then encases  herself in ice with tatsumi and explodes  overall a rather quick fight but it does  have its moments  i mean i personally thought that the way  akame overcame the time freezing skill  was a bit of a plot convenience at least  when i watched it nonetheless the fight  is still a decent way to wrap things up  for what by that point can already be  considered an original series altogether  [Music]  now here's a naruto moment that everyone  will continue remembering for years to  come  in what would eventually become his last  mission jariah runs into pain  however the leader of the enemy forces  isn't what he seems for one pain turns  out not to be just one being  but multiple puppets as expected jeriah  puts up one  hell of a fight he'd just gone through  conan but he didn't even break a sweat  given how well he kept up with the pains  in the first phase of the battle it  seemed that he could even pull it off  or escape however as strong as he may be  even the legendary jiraiya would find  himself falling against sheer numbers  he'd die in battle but not before  passing away with a smile and a peaceful  reassurance to himself  probably one of the more heroic and  heart-wrenching deaths in the series  there's a reason why i consider this  fight one of the top moments in the  entire series  period  [Music]  jyotaro finds itself at number seven on  this list  jojo's craziness doesn't seem to have  limits and all that can be seen in its  full glory in this extended battle much  of giordano'