k saw yusuke take on toguro with the  former fighting to avenge genkai toguro  dominates the battle after an initial  disadvantage which lasted for just a few  moments and the stakes get raised when  he threatens guava enraged yusuke turns  the tides and lets doguro go into his  ultimate 100  form toguro's overconfidence would be  the end of him as he charges a spirit  gun head-on leading to his muscles  crumbling and his untimely death however  it's not a regrettable death for the  villain as he thanked yusuke for  allowing him to release his full power a  memorable fight with its ups and downs  this fight is just one of the many  reasons why many old school anime fans  look back at the dark tournament arc so  fondly  ichigo has been in many fights to the  death and he's tasted death's doorstep  many times but none of those came as  memorable as the battle against all  kiara in las noches after getting bodied  by orkiora multiple times already ichigo  finally toughened his resolve and set  off to finally rescue orihime for good  thus he charges all kiyora with all of  his strength and  gets bodied again no matter which  power-up he pulls out or whichever  impressive attack  he throws he still finds himself getting  destroyed by the fourth espada at every  turn ending with him pretty much dead by  the end of it however one last power-up  a new form would come out and completely  change the complexion of the battle in  his new form it was ichigo doing the  squashing and he turns the tide so badly  that all kia ora gets a door shut on a  redemption arc attempt ichigo vs all kia  ora is out there in terms of storyline  and stakes but i think that the sheer  destructive power in this battle trumps  almost  everything that bleach had beforehand  it's also one of the most impressive  battles visually  and certainly one of the high points of  the hueco mundo arc  the first of our top three is scar vs  bradley  deep into fma brotherhood scar has  played the rival slash  uneasy ally character pretty well he  freshly turned good but i think that at  this point he still needed a fight that  would put him on the map the fight that  would define him as a character kind of  like the multiple mustang fights that  we've got when everything's said and  done  and luckily for him he gets it right  here an overwhelming strong character  king bradley finally finds his match and  eventually meets his end at the hands of  scar in a key moment in the series he  drives scar  in a corner thanks to his powers but  having lost his ultimate eye  the writing's on the wall for the  homunculus he gets his arms destroyed  before biting it you gotta give bradley  props though  even in death he still manages to  crucially stab scar and get a measure of  revenge what a way for scar to get his  character defining battle in a fight to  the death against  king bradley to boot it was an amazing  feeling to see one of the most  overpowered characters in the series  fall at the hands of scar  [Music]  [Music]  throughout the years the climactic  battle in sword of the stranger has aged  beautifully  in terms of pure spectacle though it's  one of the best sword fights that i've  ever seen  capping off what's been an amazing movie  so far nanashi and luo lang face off in  their final battle inside temple grounds  the two contrasting forces are seemingly  meant to have their final showdown and  they more than exceed  expectations with this fight after a  long drawn-out fight that has no  shortage of drama and tension nanashi  finally overcomes the seemingly  unbeatable foe and wins against luo lang  the cinematography and presentation  really drove this fight up a notch a lot  of people expected a standard sword  fight with sprinkles of drama  but got more than what they bargained  for if you need another reason to watch  sword of the stranger  may this fight be it  [Music]  and finally topping the list is none  other than a fight from one of the best  arcs in shonen  me